## Solutions

### #1: Generate a CHANGELOG from git history

This solution provides both a Claude Code skill (`SKILL.md`) and a robust bash script (`changelog.sh`) to automatically generate structured changelogs from your git commit history.

#### Setup & Usage (3 steps or fewer)
1. Place `changelog.sh` in your project root and make it executable: `chmod +x changelog.sh`
2. (Optional) Place `SKILL.md` in your `.claude/skills/generate-changelog/` directory for Claude Code integration.
3. Run the generator using Claude Code via `/generate-changelog` or directly in your terminal via `./changelog.sh`.

